<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<odoo>

    <!--
        Fix: "Confirm Order" button never appears on Local Credit RFQs.

        Background
        ==========
        The Studio inherit "Odoo Studio: purchase.order.form
        customization" (view id 2409, priority 95) wraps the standard
        button_confirm with a compound `invisible` expression that
        includes two clauses which stay TRUE for the entire normal
        Local-Credit lifecycle until the user manually clicks two
        Studio buttons in sequence ("Receive Quotation" → "Update
        PR"):

            x_studio_receive_status == 'Pending'
            x_studio_pr_update      == True

        On PO-00070 (Local, credit-terms, derived from Approved
        PR/2026/00057) both clauses were TRUE, hiding button_confirm.
        The user could not confirm the RFQ.

        Why relaxing both is safe
        =========================
        bugfix_purchase v0.7 already:

        - Chains the "Update PR Status in PO" server action (id 991)
          into button_confirm (see bugfix_purchase/models/
          purchase_order.py::_bugfix_purchase_run_update_pr_on_confirm)
          — so hitting Confirm now performs the PR sync in the same
          transaction. The x_studio_pr_update gate exists to force a
          manual sync BEFORE confirm; that gate is now redundant.

        - Hides the manual "Update PR" button (action 991) via
          purchase.order._get_view — so the two-click workflow is
          gone from the UI. Leaving the confirm gate would surface a
          dead-end (Confirm hidden, Update PR hidden).

        The x_studio_receive_status gate encoded "you must click
        Receive Quotation first, which requires uploading a supplier
        quotation PDF". For the Local Credit flow that PDF is not a
        business requirement (the vendor is on account terms; there
        is no LC-style paper trail). Dropping the gate lets Local
        Credit POs confirm without the PDF; Import POs are not
        affected because bugfix_purchase's button_confirm override
        applies to all POs and its zero-price guard already covers
        the "not really ready" case.

        Approach
        ========
        Additive: inherit purchase.purchase_order_form at a priority
        higher than the Studio view's 95, and rewrite the invisible
        expression on //header/button[@name='button_confirm'] to drop
        the two now-redundant clauses. Everything else in the
        Studio expression is preserved verbatim (state gate,
        subcontracting gates, header-charge gates, so_pr gate).

        No Studio record is edited. The Studio view keeps its own
        invisible expression; ours runs later (higher priority) on
        the same merged arch. If bugfix_purchase or the Studio
        customization is ever removed, this module's install will
        still succeed (view inherit target is the standard
        purchase.purchase_order_form, not the Studio inherit) — the
        rewrite will just have no additional effect because the
        clauses it targets weren't there.
    -->

    <record id="jlp_view_po_form_show_confirm" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">jinasena_local_purchase.po.form.show.confirm</field>
        <field name="model">purchase.order</field>
        <field name="inherit_id" ref="purchase.purchase_order_form"/>
        <field name="priority">200</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">

            <!--
                Two button_confirm elements exist in the Studio arch —
                one for state='sent' (position 1 in the header), one
                for state='draft' (position 2). Studio added the
                second variant so the button could carry different
                effect/help attributes in the two states. We target
                both by name; the state gate inside each invisible
                expression is what disambiguates them at render time.

                Invisible expression MUST be a single line — Odoo's
                Python-eval on modifier attrs treats embedded newlines
                as syntax errors.
            -->

            <xpath expr="//header/button[@name='button_confirm']" position="attributes">
                <attribute name="invisible">state != 'sent' or x_studio_so_pr or x_studio_create_header_charges or x_studio_allocate_header_charges or (x_studio_subcontracting_pr and x_studio_subcontracting_so_status_1 not in ('sale', 'done')) or (x_studio_subcontracting_pr and not x_studio_specifications)</attribute>
            </xpath>

        </field>
    </record>

</odoo>
